==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hwæt/, [ʍæt]|lang=ang}}

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|hwa-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kʷos||kʷod|lang=ang}}. Cognates include Old Frisian [[hwet]], Old Saxon [[hwat]] (Dutch [[wat]]), Old High German [[hwaz]] (German [[was]]), Old Norse [[hvat]] (Swedish [[vad]]), Gothic [[𐍈𐌰]]. The Indo-European root also led to Latin {{term|quod|lang=la}} and Lithuanian {{term|kad|kàd|lang=lt}}.

===Pronoun===
'''hwæt'''

# [[what]]

===Interjection===
'''hwæt'''

# [[what]]!, [[listen]]!

===Adverb===
'''hwæt'''

# [[now]], [[indeed]]

